  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "Because of high cycle fatigue failure of stationary blade retention cap screws, two first row (nose end) blower blade assemblies separated from the blower shroud and were ejected. One section lodged between the nose of the shroud and the end winding. Over time, vibrations resulted in the edge of the failed assembly wearing through the insulation on an A phase winding and providing a current flow path.",
    "cause_code": "X",
    "category": "Other",
    "theme": "hydrogen blower blade fatigue failure leading to generator stator ground fault",
    "provisional": false
  },
